[{"id":2892380279,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6sZjh3","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I think making `Object::has_method()` virtual should be discussed with the core team\r\n\r\nPersonally, I have kind of mixed feelings about it. This will mean that there are methods that will return `true` for `has_method()` but that won't be included in `get_method_list()`, which isn't currently the case.\r\n\r\nWe already have `JavaClass::get_java_method_list()` to list methods from Java - perhaps we should just add a `JavaClass::has_java_method()` and not mess with `Object`?","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#pullrequestreview-2892380279","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107075","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#pullrequestreview-2892380279"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107075"}},"submitted_at":"2025-06-03T13:34:58Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2892937767,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6sbron","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#pullrequestreview-2892937767","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107075","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#pullrequestreview-2892937767"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107075"}},"submitted_at":"2025-06-03T15:06:29Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2896644130,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6sp0gi","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'm not sure this is a great idea.\r\n\r\nThis would introduce a path for `Object` subclasses to define methods that are not registered in `ClassDB`, introducing 'dynamic typing' as a whole new concept to our ecosystem. Adding this would make it impossible (or at least much harder) to cache method pointers on a `Class` level, which is something I've shown in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106646 to accelerate property access by at least 60% (with potential for more).\r\n\r\nIs there some other way this could be resolved? Perhaps this is just an indication for Java functions to register their existing methods in `ClassDB` (or in the scripts way)?","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#pullrequestreview-2896644130","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107075","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#pullrequestreview-2896644130"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107075"}},"submitted_at":"2025-06-04T13:02:03Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3126214047,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc66Vj2f","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?u=25817fe797fcc7a812ba9d7f58f593f5a003abbb&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerr